
==============================================================================
1. Mobius identification: X_0(m006) = A^1-{-1,1} -> P^1-{0,1,infinity}
==============================================================================
  t=-1: u=(t+1)/2 = 0
  t=1: u=(t+1)/2 = 1
  t->infinity: u->infinity (degree-1/1 Mobius map, finite nonzero leading coeff)
  => {-1,1,infinity} maps bijectively to {0,1,infinity}: explicit
     P^1-{0,1,infinity} model confirmed.

==============================================================================
2. unit-group argument: X_0(m003) NOT isomorphic to X_0(m006) over Q
==============================================================================
  O(G_m)^x / Q^x = Z, generated by t  (X_0(m003) = A^1 - {0})
  O(A^1-{-1,1})^x / Q^x = Z^2, generated by (t-1),(t+1)  (X_0(m006))
  Free rank of the unit group modulo scalars is 1 vs 2 (= #punctures - 1
  in each case) -- a Q-isomorphism-invariant integer, so the two affine
  curves are NOT isomorphic over Q. (Cleaner than an Euler-char/pi_1
  argument since it needs no base change to C.)

